  "fields": [
    {
      "entryId": "lev-16-16",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The high priest made atonement for the holy place because of the uncleanness of the children of Israel and their transgressions. Hebrews 9:23 says the patterns of things in the heavens were purified with these sacrifices. The heavenly things themselves needed better sacrifices. Daniel 8:14 points to this same cleansing of the sanctuary at the end of the 2,300 days. First principle: the sins confessed through the year were removed from the sanctuary on the Day of Atonement. That day points to the work Christ does as our judge before He comes.",
      "density": 3.5,
      "words": 92,
      "sentences": 6,
      "maxSentenceWords": 21,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": [
          "Hebrews 9:23",
          "Daniel 8:14"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "lev-25-25",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "God gave Israel a law of redemption. If a brother grew poor and sold the land he had inherited, his nearest relative — the go'el, the kinsman-redeemer — had the duty to buy it back. Jesus became our near kinsman in the flesh. He bought back the inheritance we had lost and freed us from slavery to sin. First principle: redemption needs a close relative, a willing heart, and the full price paid.",
      "density": 3.425,
      "words": 73,
      "sentences": 5,
      "maxSentenceWords": 28,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "lev-25-10",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "God said: “And ye shall hallow the fiftieth year, and proclaim liberty throughout all the land unto all the inhabitants thereof: it shall be a jubile unto you; and ye shall return every man unto his possession…” The Jubilee is the great Old Testament type — God's advance picture of the final redemption. Lost inheritance came back, and that points to Eden restored. Debts were cancelled, and captive slaves walked free at the sound of the trumpet. First principle: redemption gives back everything that was lost in Adam.",
      "density": 3.1143,
      "words": 88,
      "sentences": 5,
      "maxSentenceWords": 16,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "lev-16-15",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "On the Day of Atonement the goat for the sin offering was killed. The high priest carried its blood inside the vail and sprinkled it on the mercy seat and in front of it. First principle: atonement needs blood brought in, not only blood shed at the altar. The blood had to be presented before God in the Most Holy Place.",
      "density": 2.725,
      "words": 61,
      "sentences": 4,
      "maxSentenceWords": 21,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "lev-16-22",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The scapegoat carried the people's sins away to a land where no one lived. First principle: the two goats together make one atonement. The first goat's blood went inside the sanctuary, and the second goat carried the sins outside. Isaiah 53 shows the same picture: one Servant carries the burden of sin.",
      "density": 2.2143,
      "words": 52,
      "sentences": 4,
      "maxSentenceWords": 16,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "lev-19-18",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "God's law forbids revenge and forbids holding a grudge. It tells each of us to love our neighbour as we love ourselves. First principle: the summary of the second table of the law begins here. The second table covers how we treat other people. Jesus, Paul, James, and the Shema prayer all build on this one command.",
      "density": 2.1679,
      "words": 57,
      "sentences": 5,
      "maxSentenceWords": 13,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "lev-24-16",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "A man who blasphemed was stoned by the whole congregation. The same law applied to the stranger and to the man born in Israel. First principle: the holiness of the LORD's Name was protected by a death sentence. Jesus fulfilled that law by dying under Israel's charge of blasphemy.",
      "density": 2.025,
      "words": 49,
      "sentences": 4,
      "maxSentenceWords": 14,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "lev-17-11",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "God gave the blood on the altar to make atonement. First principle: blood is life handed back to the One who gives life. The New Testament names the blood of Christ as the price that bought our atonement.",
      "density": 1.8071,
      "words": 38,
      "sentences": 3,
      "maxSentenceWords": 15,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "lev-26-12",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "This is the covenant promise that God will walk with His people. First principle: God walking among His people is the highest point of the covenant. Paul and John both quote this promise about the redeemed dwelling with God.",
      "density": 1.775,
      "words": 39,
      "sentences": 3,
      "maxSentenceWords": 14,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "lev-16-30",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "On that one day the people were cleansed from all their sins before the LORD. First principle: the yearly ritual cleansed the people once a year. The day it pointed to cleanses once and for all.",
      "density": 1.7571,
      "words": 36,
      "sentences": 3,
      "maxSentenceWords": 15,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
